{{!
    @template local_coursegen/preview_activity_row

    One activity a template run is going to write, in a course preview.

    The element, the classes and the nesting are an activity row's own, taken
    from core_courseformat's cm template, so the theme styles this the way it
    styles the activities beside it without being told about it.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * uid - The name the run's answer gives this activity.
    * name - What it will be called.
    * modname - Its module, which decides its colour and its icon.
    * icon - The module's rendered icon.
    * url - Where its own preview opens.
    * badge - The label saying it has not been written yet.
    * badgetip - What that label means, in full.
    * summary - What the plan says it will contain, if it has been planned.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "uid": "0f2a1c",
        "name": "Lección 1",
        "modname": "lesson",
        "icon": "<img class='icon activityicon' src='...' alt=''>",
        "url": "https://example.com/local/coursegen/activity_preview.php?sessionid=1&uid=0f2a1c",
        "badge": "AI will generate it",
        "badgetip": "This activity does not exist yet",
        "summary": "An introduction to the fundamentals."
    }
}}
<li class="activity activity-wrapper {{modname}} modtype_{{modname}} local-coursegen-planned"
    data-generation-uid="{{uid}}">
    <div class="activity-item" data-region="activity-card">
        <div class="activity-grid">
            <div class="activity-icon activityiconcontainer smaller courseicon align-self-start me-2">
                {{{icon}}}
            </div>
            <div class="activity-name-area activity-instance d-flex flex-column me-2">
                <div class="activitytitle modtype_{{modname}} position-relative align-self-start">
                    <div class="activityname">
                        <a class="aalink stretched-link" href="{{url}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                            <span class="instancename">{{name}}</span>
                        </a>
                        <span class="badge badge-light border ms-2" title="{{badgetip}}">{{badge}}</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                {{#summary}}
                <div class="activity-altcontent description mt-1">{{.}}</div>
                {{/summary}}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</li>
